"""Generic report contracts; no campaign content."""
RESEARCH = 'Work persistently toward settling the question. Test plausible answers, pursue materially different approaches when warranted, and verify the claims on which your answer depends. Do not infer the expected answer from the wording. A failed approach is useful when you record exactly what it rules out.\nMaintain a concise current checkpoint with pointers to full evidence. Distinguish established claims, conditional claims, computational evidence, conjectures, and retracted claims. Save a result before starting the next substantial step. Do not repeatedly audit the same claim without identifying a new test or unresolved issue.\nThe required deliverable is an accurate final report, whether the question is settled or not. Report completion and problem resolution are separate statuses. Never strengthen a claim to make the report look complete. A precise unresolved question is an acceptable final outcome after substantive work; it is not permission to stop investigating early. If useful work remains, take the best supported next step.'
WRITEUP = 'Write FINAL.tex now. Within your first two turns, from NOTES.md, EXPERIMENTS.md and what you already know (no new reading first), write a COMPLETE first draft of the report; then read only what you need to repair it, saving after each repair. The harness compiles FINAL.tex every few minutes and sends you any LaTeX errors; fix them first. If you cannot write the whole draft at once, your first write should be a small valid document stating the current status, what is established, and the exact unresolved obligations. Write an initial AUDIT.md at the same time; mark unchecked items as unchecked. A skeleton is a rescue checkpoint, not a finished report.\nDo not resolve an open issue as a prerequisite to writing it down. If evidence is missing or contradictory, state that limitation and downgrade or omit the affected claim. Expand the report from saved evidence. Only checks needed to assess claims already in the report are allowed; an old unfinished research plan does not automatically qualify as a check. No new broad search, substantial new implementation, or replacement line of attack. Record promising unfinished work in BLOCKED.md.\nThis mode supersedes research instructions requiring further exploration before writing. It survives session restarts. The original deadline and cumulative budget still apply.'
AUDIT = 'Read the draft as a referee, not as its author. First check the strongest claim and the step that connects the supporting work to the requested conclusion. Check every quantifier, hypothesis, and claimed equivalence; distinguish a sufficient condition from a necessary one. Verify source applicability against the exact saved source. Inspect whether tests check the claimed assertion or a weaker surrogate.\nRepair or downgrade unsupported claims, reconcile the opening status with the body and BLOCKED.md, complete attribution, and run the actual document build if available. Record a build failure or unavailable dependency honestly; a marker check is not a build. Improve exposition only after these checks. Do not invent work to fill the allocation. Save before the next session wall.'
BLOCKED = 'BLOCKED.md must identify: the exact unresolved statement with its hypotheses and scope; which established claims depend on it; proof or source locations for the surviving results; materially different approaches tried and why they failed; the strongest contrary evidence and retractions; the best concrete next step with its expected discriminating outcome; and why that step cannot usefully be completed within the available resources. Distinguish a research obstacle from a tool, source-access, or resource failure. Do not call a question open in the literature merely because this run did not settle it.\nWriting BLOCKED.md does not end the run. A terminal blocked claim requests verification. If a feasible, informative next step remains, continue it in research mode; during write-up, preserve it for follow-up and finish the report. A verifier may accept an honestly limited report without certifying the unresolved assertion or proving impossibility.'
VERIFY = "Check FINAL.tex and the underlying evidence before treating earlier audit verdicts as evidence. Evaluate report completeness and claimed resolution separately. For a completion claim, identify and test the most vulnerable dependency; for a blocked claim, check the remaining question's precision, the validity and scope of the reduction, and whether an untried feasible step would be informative. Do not equate repeated agreement by this same model with independent validation.\nReturn one of: supported completion; supported partial report with unresolved question; concrete actionable defect; insufficient verification resources. Cite the private evidence for the decision. The public event contains only the status and reason category. No missing report pair can pass delivery. Do not restart research after write-up became sticky; repair or downgrade within the remaining allocation."
BUILD = 'Compile FINAL.tex with `latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error FINAL.tex` and fix every error. Missing packages are environment limitations: report them, never delete content to hide them. TeX is offline; do not download packages.'

VERIFY += ' Write VERIFICATION.json with outcome (supported-completion, supported-partial, concrete-actionable-defect, or insufficient-verification-resources), reason_category (supported, unsupported-claim, invalid-reduction, status-mismatch, placeholder, missing-audit, missing-dependency, feasible-next-step, or resources), and private evidence pointers. A supported-partial verdict requires an accurate reviewable report; it does not certify the unresolved assertion. Only supported outcomes complete this verification goal.'

try: from .settings import PAGE_LIMIT
except ImportError: from settings import PAGE_LIMIT
OUTPUT = (f'Write FINAL.tex in the format of SOLUTION-TEMPLATE.tex, at most {PAGE_LIMIT} pages. '
          'Keep 12pt article and optional plain fullpage; do not change layout, line spacing, or body font size. '
          'Shorten the exposition to fit. Wrong claims score negatively and a blank answer does not, '
          'so state exactly what is proved and what is open. Attribution is scored, so cite exactly.')

def campaign_goal(web_instructions):
    return RESEARCH+'\n\n'+BLOCKED+'\n\n'+OUTPUT+'\n\nRead PROBLEM.md for this run’s question.\n\n'+web_instructions
